<description>
Collapse the right-edge palette into one vertical coded bar using the grey marker height as the per-color run length.

Input structure
The grid has a dominant background, one top-aligned vertical grey marker
segment, and a contiguous set of full-height non-background palette columns
at the right edge. The column immediately to the left of the palette is
background.

Rule
Read the palette columns left-to-right. Erase those palette columns, then
fill the adjacent background column with the palette colors from top to
bottom, repeating each palette color for as many rows as the grey marker
segment is tall and cycling through the palette until the grid ends.

Key insight
The grey segment is not copied; its height is the run-length instruction
for expanding the ordered right-edge palette into the new vertical bar.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "right-edge full-height palette columns s read left-to-right",
  "dst": "runs in the single background column immediately left of the palette, ordered top-to-bottom",
  "match_cond": "s at palette rank k fills each destination run whose run index mod palette length is k",
  "transform": "erase the original palette columns; fill the target column runs with their assigned palette colors and preserve the grey marker",
  "symbol_instructions": "top-aligned grey marker height gives the run length for every palette color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 5-14 rows x 5-9 cols, background always black (0)
  grey_marker:
    position: column 0, top-aligned (rows 0..run_len-1)
    height: 1-4 (this is the run_len parameter)
    rest of column 0 below marker is background
  palette:
    count: 2-3 full-height single-color columns, contiguous at right edge
    colors: distinct, non-black, non-grey
    order: left-to-right determines cycling order
  layout: >=1 background-only columns between marker col and first palette col [observed 2-5]
  rest_of_grid: all cells outside marker and palette are background
  output:
    same grid size; palette columns erased to background
    target column (immediately left of palette) filled top-to-bottom with palette colors
    each color repeated run_len rows, cycling through palette until grid ends

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is fully determined by a few parameters)
  steps:
    1. Pick H in [5,14], num_palette P in [2,3], run_len R in [1,4]
    2. Pick gap G >= 1 such that W = 1 + G + 1 + P (marker_col + gap + target_col + palette) is in [5,9]
    3. Create H x W grid of black
    4. Place grey marker in col 0, rows 0..R-1
    5. Choose P distinct colors (not black, not grey); fill rightmost P columns each as full-height solid color
    6. Target col = W - P - 1; leave it black (will be filled in output)
    7. Output = copy input, erase palette cols, fill target col with cycling palette repeated R rows each
