    3. Build each nesting tree inside-out. Start from innermost (smallest) rect,
       assign unique color within the tree. Place each parent around child with
       >=0 gap on each side (>=1 preferred). Parent must be >= child + 2 on each
       axis to have interior.
    4. Place outermost rects on grid with >=1 cell gap to grid edge and no overlap
       between trees. One may touch grid edge (gap=0) rarely.
    5. To build output, copy input then for each outermost rect with children,
       recolor all non-bg pixels inside its bbox to the outermost color.
